<Layout 
  title="Dark Matter Galaxy Evolution Observations Dark Matter Galaxy Rotation Cheat Sheet | Free Rotation Curves, Mass Distribution"
  description="Complete dark matter galaxy evolution observations dark matter galaxy rotation cheat sheet with rotation curves and mass distribution. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Dark Matter Galaxy Evolution Observations Dark Matter Galaxy Rotation<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Rotation curves and mass distribution. From observed velocities to dark matter halos.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Rotation Curves</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Expected vs Observed</h3>
        <pre><code>Expected: v ∝ 1/√r (Keplerian)
Observed: v ≈ const (flat)
Evidence: rotation curves of spiral galaxies
Implies: M(r) ∝ r (dark matter halo)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Mass Decomposition</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Components</h3>
        <pre><code>Stellar disk: dominates inner regions
Gas disk: contributes ~ 10% of mass
Dark matter halo: dominates outer regions
Bulge: contributes in central regions
Total: sum of all components</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dark Matter Fraction</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Fractions</h3>
        <pre><code>Milky Way: ~ 85% dark matter
Dwarf galaxies: ~ 99% dark matter
Elliptical galaxies: ~ 80% dark matter
Clusters: ~ 85% dark matter
Universal average: ~ 27% of total energy</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Alternative Explanations</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>MOND</h3>
        <pre><code>Modified Newtonian Dynamics
a < a₀: gravity modified
Fits rotation curves without dark matter
Struggles with clusters and CMB
Not a relativistic theory</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
